-- title:
--   Unrolling a linear level recursion
-- statement:
--   Let $s \ge 2$, $E \ge 0$, and $D : \mathbb N \to \mathbb R$ with $D(0) \ge 0$ and $D(k+1) \le E + s\,D(k)$ for all $k$. Then
--
--   $$D(k) \le (E + D(0))\,(2 s^{k} - 1) \qquad \text{for all } k.$$
--
--   In Lean:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem R6.level_unroll (E : ℝ) (s : ℕ) (D : ℕ → ℝ) (hs : 2 ≤ s) (hE : 0 ≤ E) (hD0 : 0 ≤ D 0)
--       (hstep : ∀ k, D (k + 1) ≤ E + s * D k) :
--       ∀ k, D k ≤ (E + D 0) * (2 * (s : ℝ) ^ k - 1)
--   ```
